			"Message": "refactor(Mist): Rename entry point to PascalCase and expand lint allowances\n\nAlign the Mist component's Rust source structure with CodeEditorLand's strict PascalCase naming convention by renaming the library entry point from `Source/lib.rs` to `Source/Library.rs` and updating `Cargo.toml` to reflect the new path.\n\nConsolidate all lint suppressions into the single root file. Merge `clippy::tabs_in_doc_comments` and `clippy::unnecessary_lazy_evaluations` into the primary `#![allow(...)]` block alongside existing foreign-type allowances (`non_snake_case`, `non_camel_case_types`, `non_upper_case_globals`). Additionally, add `dead_code`, `unused_imports`, `unused_variables`, and `unused_assignments` to accommodate ongoing feature development without visual noise in sub-modules.\n\nThis ensures the file structure matches project-wide naming standards and centralizes temporary development allowances at the library root.",
			"SHA": "9268b035d7156d65d7d305a05ad2857feb1be4b7"
		},
