				"⣿⡇⠀⠀⠀",
				20,
				6
			],
			"Message": "style(Mist): Remove unnecessary `non_snake_case` allow attributes\n\nClean up Rust lint suppressions in Mist core modules by removing the `non_snake_case` flag from `#![allow(...)]` directives. The naming conventions in `ForwardSecurity.rs`, `Resolver.rs`, `Server.rs`, `WebSocket.rs`, and `Zone.rs` now comply with Rust's snake_case standard for functions and variables, making the exceptions for foreign types (`non_camel_case_types`) and constants (`non_upper_case_globals`) sufficient.\n\nAlso update the `Documentation/Rust` submodule pointer to sync with upstream changes. This reduces code clutter and aligns with strict Rust style guidelines.",
